# =============================================================================
# throat_2D_L850um_eps0.33um_narrowL_deadend: the 0c-C1 two-throat pore on a
# finer mesh, for the eps-convergence pair of plan issue 1 (2026-11-06).
#
# Identical walls, plugs and boundary faces to
# throat_2D_L850um_eps0.86um_narrowL_deadend.opts (checked field by field);
# only eps, the mesh and dtmax change:
#   comp_eps.py --Lx 8.5e-4 --Ly 1.6e-4 --Rave 1.5e-5 --T0 -20 --alpha 1e-2 --vn 1.95e-9
#   -> eps 3.2780e-07 m, Nx 3668, Ny 691, tau_sub 89.299 s, dtmax = 2 tau_sub
#   (v_n 1.95e-9 m/s: the narrow-plug front speed measured in 0c-C1).
# Mesh: preprocess/build_geometry_two_throat.py --eps 3.278e-7 --tag narrow_left_eps0.328
# Question: does the narrow-plug vanishing time move by less than 5 % from the
# 0.86 um mesh (where Pi ~ 1.0-1.3)? If so, keep 0.86 um for production.
# =============================================================================
# DOF_GRID: 3670 693
